.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/engine.io-client Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "Engine\&.IO client"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
This is the client for \fREngine\&.IO\fP, the implementation of transport-based cross-browser/cross-device bi-directional communication layer for \fRSocket\&.IO\fP\&.
.SH "How to use"
.PP
.SS "Standalone"
You can find an \fRengine\&.io\&.js\fP file in this repository, which is a standalone build you can use as follows:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src="/path/to/engine\&.io\&.js"></script>
<script>
  // eio = Socket
  const socket = eio('ws://localhost');
  socket\&.on('open', () => {
    socket\&.on('message', (data) => {});
    socket\&.on('close', () => {});
  });
</script>
.fi
.PP
.SS "With browserify"
Engine\&.IO is a commonjs module, which means you can include it by using \fRrequire\fP on the browser and package using \fRbrowserify\fP:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
install the client package

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install engine\&.io\-client
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
write your app code

.PP
.PP
.nf
const { Socket } = require('engine\&.io\-client');
const socket = new Socket('ws://localhost');
socket\&.on('open', () => {
  socket\&.on('message', (data) => {});
  socket\&.on('close', () => {});
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
build your app bundle

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ browserify app\&.js > bundle\&.js
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
include on your page

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src="/path/to/bundle\&.js"></script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
.SS "Sending and receiving binary"
.PP
.nf
<script src="/path/to/engine\&.io\&.js"></script>
<script>
  const socket = eio('ws://localhost/');
  socket\&.binaryType = 'blob';
  socket\&.on('open', () => {
    socket\&.send(new Int8Array(5));
    socket\&.on('message', (blob) => {});
    socket\&.on('close', () => {});
  });
</script>
.fi
.PP
.SS "Node\&.JS"
Add \fRengine\&.io-client\fP to your \fRpackage\&.json\fP and then:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const { Socket } = require('engine\&.io\-client');
const socket = new Socket('ws://localhost');
socket\&.on('open', () => {
  socket\&.on('message', (data) => {});
  socket\&.on('close', () => {});
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "Node\&.js with certificates"
.PP
.nf
const opts = {
  key: fs\&.readFileSync('test/fixtures/client\&.key'),
  cert: fs\&.readFileSync('test/fixtures/client\&.crt'),
  ca: fs\&.readFileSync('test/fixtures/ca\&.crt')
};

const { Socket } = require('engine\&.io\-client');
const socket = new Socket('ws://localhost', opts);
socket\&.on('open', () => {
  socket\&.on('message', (data) => {});
  socket\&.on('close', () => {});
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "Node\&.js with extraHeaders"
.PP
.nf
const opts = {
  extraHeaders: {
    'X\-Custom\-Header\-For\-My\-Project': 'my\-secret\-access\-token',
    'Cookie': 'user_session=NI2JlCKF90aE0sJZD9ZzujtdsUqNYSBYxzlTsvdSUe35ZzdtVRGqYFr0kdGxbfc5gUOkR9RGp20GVKza; path=/; expires=Tue, 07\-Apr\-2015 18:18:08 GMT; secure; HttpOnly'
  }
};

const { Socket } = require('engine\&.io\-client');
const socket = new Socket('ws://localhost', opts);
socket\&.on('open', () => {
  socket\&.on('message', (data) => {});
  socket\&.on('close', () => {});
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
In the browser, the \fRWebSocket\fP object does not support additional headers\&. In case you want to add some headers as part of some authentication mechanism, you can use the \fRtransportOptions\fP attribute\&. Please note that in this case the headers won't be sent in the WebSocket upgrade request\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// WILL NOT WORK in the browser
const socket = new Socket('http://localhost', {
  extraHeaders: {
    'X\-Custom\-Header\-For\-My\-Project': 'will not be sent'
  }
});
// WILL NOT WORK
const socket = new Socket('http://localhost', {
  transports: ['websocket'], // polling is disabled
  transportOptions: {
    polling: {
      extraHeaders: {
        'X\-Custom\-Header\-For\-My\-Project': 'will not be sent'
      }
    }
  }
});
// WILL WORK
const socket = new Socket('http://localhost', {
  transports: ['polling', 'websocket'],
  transportOptions: {
    polling: {
      extraHeaders: {
        'X\-Custom\-Header\-For\-My\-Project': 'will be used'
      }
    }
  }
});
.fi
.PP
.SH "Features"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Lightweight
.IP "\(bu" 2
Runs on browser and node\&.js seamlessly
.IP "\(bu" 2
Transports are independent of \fREngine\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Easy to debug
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Easy to unit test
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
Runs inside HTML5 WebWorker
.IP "\(bu" 2
Can send and receive binary data
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Receives as ArrayBuffer or Blob when in browser, and Buffer or ArrayBuffer in Node
.IP "  \(bu" 4
When XHR2 or WebSockets are used, binary is emitted directly\&. Otherwise binary is encoded into base64 strings, and decoded when binary types are supported\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
With browsers that don't support ArrayBuffer, an object { base64: true, data: dataAsBase64String } is emitted on the \fRmessage\fP event\&.
.PP

.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "Socket"
The client class\&. Mixes in \fREmitter\fP\&. Exposed as \fReio\fP in the browser standalone build\&.
.SS "Properties"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRprotocol\fP \fI(Number)\fP: protocol revision number
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRbinaryType\fP \fI(String)\fP : can be set to 'arraybuffer' or 'blob' in browsers, and \fRbuffer\fP or \fRarraybuffer\fP in Node\&. Blob is only used in browser if it's supported\&.
.PP
.SS "Events"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRopen\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon successful connection\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRmessage\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired when data is received from the server\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBArguments\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP | \fRArrayBuffer\fP: utf-8 encoded data or ArrayBuffer containing binary data
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRclose\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon disconnection\&. In compliance with the WebSocket API spec, this event may be fired even if the \fRopen\fP event does not occur (i\&.e\&. due to connection error or \fRclose()\fP)\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRerror\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired when an error occurs\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRflush\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon completing a buffer flush
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdrain\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired after \fRdrain\fP event of transport if writeBuffer is empty
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRupgradeError\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired if an error occurs with a transport we're trying to upgrade to\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRupgrade\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon upgrade success, after the new transport is set
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRping\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon receiving a ping packet\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpong\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Fired upon \fIflushing\fP a pong packet (ie: actual packet write out)
.PP

.PP
.SS "Methods"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBconstructor\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Initializes the client
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP uri
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRObject\fP: optional, options object
.PP

.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBOptions\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRagent\fP (\fRhttp\&.Agent\fP): \fRhttp\&.Agent\fP to use, defaults to \fRfalse\fP (NodeJS only)
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRupgrade\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): defaults to true, whether the client should try to upgrade the transport from long-polling to something better\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRforceBase64\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): forces base 64 encoding for polling transport even when XHR2 responseType is available and WebSocket even if the used standard supports binary\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRwithCredentials\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): defaults to \fRfalse\fP, whether to include credentials (cookies, authorization headers, TLS client certificates, etc\&.) with cross-origin XHR polling requests\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRtimestampRequests\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): whether to add the timestamp with each transport request\&. Note: polling requests are always stamped unless this option is explicitly set to \fRfalse\fP (\fRfalse\fP)
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRtimestampParam\fP (\fRString\fP): timestamp parameter (\fRt\fP)
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRpath\fP (\fRString\fP): path to connect to, default is \fR/engine\&.io\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRtransports\fP (\fRArray\fP): a list of transports to try (in order)\&. Defaults to \fR['polling', 'websocket', 'webtransport']\fP\&. \fREngine\fP always attempts to connect directly with the first one, provided the feature detection test for it passes\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRtransportOptions\fP (\fRObject\fP): hash of options, indexed by transport name, overriding the common options for the given transport
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRrememberUpgrade\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): defaults to false\&. If true and if the previous websocket connection to the server succeeded, the connection attempt will bypass the normal upgrade process and will initially try websocket\&. A connection attempt following a transport error will use the normal upgrade process\&. It is recommended you turn this on only when using SSL/TLS connections, or if you know that your network does not block websockets\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRpfx\fP (\fRString\fP|\fRBuffer\fP): Certificate, Private key and CA certificates to use for SSL\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRkey\fP (\fRString\fP): Private key to use for SSL\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRpassphrase\fP (\fRString\fP): A string of passphrase for the private key or pfx\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRcert\fP (\fRString\fP): Public x509 certificate to use\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRca\fP (\fRString\fP|\fRArray\fP): An authority certificate or array of authority certificates to check the remote host against\&.\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRciphers\fP (\fRString\fP): A string describing the ciphers to use or exclude\&. Consult the \fRcipher format list\fP for details on the format\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRrejectUnauthorized\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): If true, the server certificate is verified against the list of supplied CAs\&. An 'error' event is emitted if verification fails\&. Verification happens at the connection level, before the HTTP request is sent\&. Can be used in Node\&.js client environment to manually specify certificate information\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRperMessageDeflate\fP (\fRObject|Boolean\fP): parameters of the WebSocket permessage-deflate extension (see \fRws module\fP api docs)\&. Set to \fRfalse\fP to disable\&. (\fRtrue\fP)
.IP "      \(bu" 8
\fRthreshold\fP (\fRNumber\fP): data is compressed only if the byte size is above this value\&. This option is ignored on the browser\&. (\fR1024\fP)
.PP

.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRextraHeaders\fP (\fRObject\fP): Headers that will be passed for each request to the server (via xhr-polling and via websockets)\&. These values then can be used during handshake or for special proxies\&. Can only be used in Node\&.js client environment\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRlocalAddress\fP (\fRString\fP): the local IP address to connect to
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRautoUnref\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): whether the transport should be \fRunref\fP'd upon creation\&. This calls \fRunref\fP on the underlying timers and sockets so that the program is allowed to exit if they are the only timers/sockets in the event system (Node\&.js only)
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRuseNativeTimers\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): Whether to always use the native timeouts\&. This allows the client to reconnect when the native timeout functions are overridden, such as when mock clocks are installed with \fR\fR@sinonjs/fake-timers\fP\fP\&.
.PP

.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBPolling-only options\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRrequestTimeout\fP (\fRNumber\fP): Timeout for xhr-polling requests in milliseconds (\fR0\fP)
.PP

.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBWebsocket-only options\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRprotocols\fP (\fRArray\fP): a list of subprotocols (see \fRMDN reference\fP)
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRcloseOnBeforeunload\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): whether to silently close the connection when the \fR\fRbeforeunload\fP\fP event is emitted in the browser (defaults to \fRfalse\fP)
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsend\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Sends a message to the server
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP | \fRArrayBuffer\fP | \fRArrayBufferView\fP | \fRBlob\fP: data to send
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRObject\fP: optional, options object
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRFunction\fP: optional, callback upon \fRdrain\fP
.PP

.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBOptions\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRcompress\fP (\fRBoolean\fP): whether to compress sending data\&. This option is ignored and forced to be \fRtrue\fP on the browser\&. (\fRtrue\fP)
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRclose\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Disconnects the client\&.
.PP

.PP
.SS "Transport"
The transport class\&. Private\&. \fIInherits from EventEmitter\fP\&.
.SS "Events"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpoll\fP: emitted by polling transports upon starting a new request
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpollComplete\fP: emitted by polling transports upon completing a request
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdrain\fP: emitted by polling transports upon a buffer drain
.PP
.SH "Tests"
.PP
\fRengine\&.io-client\fP is used to test \fRengine\fP\&. Running the \fRengine\&.io\fP test suite ensures the client works and vice-versa\&.

.PP
Browser tests are run using \fRzuul\fP\&. You can run the tests locally using the following command\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
\&./node_modules/\&.bin/zuul \-\-local 8080 \-\- test/index\&.js
.fi
.PP

.PP
Additionally, \fRengine\&.io-client\fP has a standalone test suite you can run with \fRmake test\fP which will run node\&.js and browser tests\&. You must have zuul setup with a saucelabs account\&.
.SH "Support"
.PP
The support channels for \fRengine\&.io-client\fP are the same as \fRsocket\&.io\fP:
.IP "\(bu" 2
irc\&.freenode\&.net **#socket\&.io**
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRGoogle Groups\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRWebsite\fP
.PP
.SH "Development"
.PP
To contribute patches, run tests or benchmarks, make sure to clone the repository:

.PP
.PP
.nf
git clone git://github\&.com/socketio/engine\&.io\-client\&.git
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then:

.PP
.PP
.nf
cd engine\&.io\-client
npm install
.fi
.PP

.PP
See the \fRTests\fP section above for how to run tests before submitting any patches\&.
